    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1209">

                <pb facs="1255" n="1241" xml:id="pg1241"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.77/1942: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Messersmith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-10T11:00:00-05:00">March 10, 1944—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 14—10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–743. The President,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1209-f1"/> using his extraordinary
                    war powers, has issued a decree amending certain portions of the laws governing
                    the administration of the National Railways of Mexico.</p>
                <p>This decree strengthens the powers of the General Manager in regard to
                    organization, administration and personnel matters, and, more important,
                    provides that the General Manager shall have the authority to dictate
                    regulations to replace the stipulations in the workers’ contract whenever the
                    latter in his opinion obstruct or endanger the successful operation of the
                    railroads.</p>
                <p>The text and translation of this decree will be forwarded as soon as the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Diario Oficial</hi> is available.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d1209-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Messersmith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1209-f1" n="2" xml:id="d1209-f1-content">
                <p>Manuel Avila Camacho.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1209-f2" n="3" xml:id="d1209-f2-content">
                <p>This decree of March 9, published in the <hi rendition="#italic">Diario
                        Oficial</hi> of March 11, 1944, is generally referred to as the Railroad
                    Reform Decree of March 11.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
